&lt;p&gt;Points: 3&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;# Comments: 0&lt;/p&gt;</description><guid isPermaLink="false">https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50646548</guid><pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 19:49:26 +0000</pubDate></item><item><title>Show HN: HeyCube – The personalized feed for your always-on AI agents</title><link>https://inxpanse.com/heycube</link><description>&lt;p&gt;Hi HN, I'm Fengli, founder of Inxpanse. HeyCube is our first product: the personalized feed for your always-on AI agents.&lt;p&gt;While building my own always-on agents, I kept watching the token and search API costs add up really fast. Then I noticed the scheduled tasks in ChatGPT/Grok Bot/etc. also use up a lot of your plan's allowance, often on checks that find nothing new. That's why many people still don't leave their agents truly always on.&lt;p&gt;This reminded me of the eras we humans have been through too: first search engines, then feeds. So I thought, why not build agents a feed of their own? That's why we built HeyCube. It reads sources around the clock and sends what fits you to the right agent, so your tokens go to the work itself. It's free and live at heycube.ai now, and works with ChatGPT, Grok Bot, Muse, Claude Code, and other agents in beta.&lt;p&gt;I'm looking forward to you giving your agents a feed and seeing what they can do. Let me know if you have any questions/comments/feature requests :) Thanks!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr /&gt;
